# BASELINE .gitignore -- canonical source, synced into each repo as `.gitignore`.
#
# Extracted 2026-07-29 (S4) from tcp-supabase/.gitignore, keeping only what applies to ANY repo.
# A consuming repo appends its own project-specific entries below the marker at the end.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS ALONGSIDE ~/.gitignore_global. `core.excludesfile` already points at
# ~/.gitignore_global, which covers these with ZERO copies on this machine -- and that is the
# better mechanism where it applies. But it is MACHINE-LOCAL: a clone on any other machine, or a
# CI runner, gets none of it. So the portable rules are committed per repo and the global file
# stays for operator conveniences that should not be imposed on a clone.

# --- Language and tooling caches ---------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Editor and OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp

# --- Claude Code -------------------------------------------------------------
# Subagent isolated worktrees. Transient, auto-removed when the agent finishes.
.claude/worktrees/

# Machine-local permission overrides. NEVER committed: they encode one operator's
# allow-list and would silently WIDEN permissions for anyone else who clones the
# repo. This is the entry most worth understanding rather than copying -- a
# committed settings.local.json is a privilege escalation that looks like config.
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Working files -----------------------------------------------------------
# Session scratch: temp and secret-bearing working files. Never committed.
.scratch/

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Belt and braces. A .env that reaches a commit is a rotation event, not a revert.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/.env

# --- Build output ------------------------------------------------------------
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# =============================================================================
# sync-repo-files.py replaces everything ABOVE the marker line below, and
# preserves everything AFTER it, so a repo keeps its own ignores across syncs.
#
# The marker MUST be the last line this file owns. An earlier version put these
# explanatory lines BELOW it, so every sync carried them forward while the
# baseline re-supplied them -- the file grew on each run. A sync that is not
# idempotent is not a sync, it is an append.
#
# Do not remove or reword the marker, and do not add anything after it here.
# =============================================================================
# REPO-SPECIFIC ENTRIES BELOW THIS LINE
# --- carried over from this repo's pre-sync .gitignore (S4 first sync) ---
# Environment files
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.development
.env.test
.env.production

# API keys and secrets
*.key
*.pem
secrets.json
config/secrets.yml
.secrets

# OS files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Editor files
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.project
.classpath
.settings/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
.yarn/
lerna-debug.log*
*.tgz

# Build outputs
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo
.cache/

# Test coverage
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Task files (Claude Code teams)
tasks/

# Personal configs (if any)
personal/
private/

# Session templates (not committed)
examples/sessions/*.tmp

# Local drafts
marketing/
.dmux/
.dmux-hooks/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.backup

# Observer temp files (continuous-learning-v2)
.observer-tmp/

# Rust build artifacts
ecc2/target/

# Bootstrap pipeline outputs
# Generated lock files in tool subdirectories
.opencode/package-lock.json
.opencode/node_modules/

# yarn is the canonical package manager for this repo (see package.json
# "packageManager"); ignore stray lockfiles from running another manager locally
/bun.lock
/bun.lockb
assets/images/security/badrudi-exploit.mp4

.aider*
